      array['Describe a colour using hue, saturation and value', 'Build a monochromatic and an analogous colour scheme', 'Recognise the colour mistakes beginners most often make'],
      'This one is tool-agnostic — no software on screen, just the principles, which is exactly right for a first pass.

Every colour breaks down into three things: **hue** (which colour it is), **saturation** (how intense) and **value** (how light or dark). Almost every "my design looks wrong but I don''t know why" moment comes from value: two colours at the same value sit on top of each other and the design goes flat, no matter how nice the hues are.

