Negative space is the empty area around and between your elements, and treating it as a deliberate choice rather than leftover is one of the clearest markers of experience. Beginners fill space because it feels wasteful; the result is a design with nowhere for the eye to rest.

**Scale** is the most direct hierarchy tool you have. Make the most important thing genuinely, obviously bigger — not slightly bigger. A viewer decides what to look at first in well under a second, and size is what decides it for them. If everything on your design is roughly the same size, you have not told the viewer anything about what matters.',
      'Take a design where everything is a similar size. Pick the one message that matters most, make it dramatically larger, and shrink everything else. Then increase the margins substantially. Compare against the original.',
