A grid is a set of invisible columns and margins that everything aligns to. It is the reason professional layouts feel calm: alignment stops being a per-element decision and becomes automatic. It is also what makes a *set* of designs look related — same grid, different content, and a series holds together with no extra effort.

Grids are a tool, not a cage. Deliberately breaking the grid for one element is a genuine technique for drawing attention — but it only reads as deliberate if the rest of the design obeys the grid. Break it everywhere and you just have a mess.

This video covers grids specifically; the white-space side of the same story is in the two previous lessons.',
